english_text:
Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yahya from Abu Ja’far from his father from Hafs ibn Ghiyath from Imam Ja’far {a.s}
from his father {a.s}, Imam al-Baqir {a.s}, peace be upon them both, he said:
Imam al-Baqir {a.s} said: “The third adhan on the day of Friday is an innovation (bidah).”

Muhammad ibn Ahmad ibn Yahya from Ibn Abi Ishaq from al-Nawfali from al-Sakuni from Imam Ja’far {a.s}
from his father, Imam al-Baqir {a.s}, peace be upon them both, from Imam Ali {a.s}, peace be upon him:
Imam Ali {a.s} said: “The slave (abd) should not lead (in prayer) except his own
household.”

Then you perform two units of prayer and say:
“O’ Allah {SWT}, You {AZJ} are exalted in status, mighty in dominion, severe in strength,
magnificent in majesty, powerful, overwhelming, near in mercy, true in promise,
faithful in covenant, near, responsive, hearer of supplication, acceptor of repentance,
enumerator of what You {AZJ} have created, capable of what You {AZJ} will, perceiver of
whomever You {AZJ} pursue, provider for whomever You {AZJ} create, grateful when
thanked, mindful when remembered.
So I ask You {AZJ}, O’ my God {AZJ}, as one in need;
and I turn to You {AZJ} as a poor one;
and I humble myself to You {AZJ} as one in fear;
and I weep to You {AZJ} as one distressed;
and I hope in You {AZJ} as a helper;
and I seek forgiveness from You {AZJ} as one weak;
and I rely upon You {AZJ} seeking reward;
and I seek provision from You {AZJ} with open hope.
And I ask You {AZJ}, O’ my God {AZJ}, to send blessings upon (Prophet) Muhammad {saws}
and the family of Muhammad {saws}, and that You {AZJ} forgive me my sins, accept my
deeds, ease my return, and bring relief to my heart. My God {AZJ}, I ask You {AZJ} to confirm
my hope, pardon my sin, and protect me from disobedience.
My God {AZJ}, I have grown weak, and I have no strength; I have become incapable, and
I have no power. My God {AZJ}, I have come to You {AZJ} as one who has wronged his own
soul, acknowledging the evil of my deeds. I have remembered my heedlessness and
become fearful of what I have done.
So send blessings upon (Prophet) Muhammad {saws} and the family of Muhammad {saws},
be pleased with me, and fulfill all of my needs of this world and the Hereafter, O’ Most
Merciful of the merciful.”

As for what was narrated by Ahmad ibn Muhammad ibn Isa from Muhammad ibn Ismail ibn Buzay from his
uncle Hamzah ibn Buzay from Ali ibn Suwayd from al-Ridha {a.s}, peace be upon him, as we understand, he
said:
Imam al-Ridha {a.s} said: “In the prayer over the deceased (Salat Al Mayyit), you recite
in the first (takbir) Surah al-Fatihah;
in the second (takbir), you send blessings upon the Prophet {saws}, may Allah {SWT} bless
him and his family;
in the third (takbir), you supplicate for the believing men and believing women;
in the fourth (takbir), you supplicate for your deceased;
and the fifth (takbir) is the one by which you conclude.”

Ahmad ibn Muhammad, from Muhammad ibn Sinan, from Hammad ibn Uthman and Khalaf ibn Hammad,
from Rub'i ibn Abdillah and Al-Fudayl ibn Yasar, from Abu Abdillah {a.s}, peace be upon him, who said:
Imam al-Sadiq {a.s} said: “There is no (prayer of) Jumu'ah, nor Fitr, nor Adha in travel.”

Ali ibn al-Hasan ibn Faddal from Muhammad ibn Ali from Muhammad ibn Yahya from Ghiyath ibn Ibrahim
from Abu Abdillah {a.s}, peace be upon him, from his father {a.s}, peace be upon him, who said:
Imam {a.s} said: “There is no funeral prayer over a bier, that has a woman with it.”

From him, from Muhammad ibn al-Walid from Yunus ibn Ya'qub from Abu Abdillah {a.s}, peace be upon him,
who said:
I asked Imam al-Sadiq {a.s} about a funeral that I did not catch, until it reached the grave.
Should I pray over it?
Imam {a.s} said: “If you reach it before it is buried, then if you wish, you may pray over
it.”
COMPLETION OF VOLUME THREE
Praise be to Allah {SWT} {SWT}, the Lord {AZJ} of the worlds.
ACKNOWLEDGEMENT
English translation of Volume 3 - Edition 1 [2025] of the book "Tahdib Al Ahkam" has
been completed, authored by Shaykh Al-Saeed Abu Ja'far Muhammad ibn Al-Hasan
Al-Tusi, may Allah {SWT} sanctify his soul and illuminate his grave.
We present our translational efforts in the service of our Imam al-Zaman, Imam
Muhammad ibn Hassan Al-Mahdi; Al-Qa'im; Al-Hujjah; Al-Muntazar; Al-Khalaf al-
Salih; Al-Maw'ud; Baqiyatullah; Sahib al-Zaman and His Infallible Forefathers {a.s}.
And praise be to Allah {SWT}, the Lord {AZJ} of the worlds, and blessings [and peace] be
upon our Masters Prophet Muhammad {saws} and his pure progeny, and his successor,
the Commander of the Faithful Imam Ali ibn Abi Talib {a.s}.
Here we conclude our word on this Volume 3 - Edition 1 [2025].
Praise be to Allah {SWT}, the Lord {AZJ} of the worlds.
Ya Allah {SWT} - Ya Ar-Rahmaan (The Beneficent) & Ar-Raheem (The Merciful), Ya Dhul-Jalaali-Wal-Ikram.
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Maajid (The Illustrious, the Magnificent) & Al-Mumeet (The Creator of Death);
by the waseelah of Mohammad Al Mustafa {saws}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Awwal (The First) & Al-Akhir (The Last);
by the waseelah of Ali Al Murtaza {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Fattaah (Chief Judge) & Al Fatiras-Samawati wal-ardh (Maker of Heavens & Earth);
by the waseelah of Fatima tuz Zahra {s.a}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Haleem (The Most Forbearing) & Al-Hakeem (The All Wise);
by the waseelah of Hassan Al Mujtaba {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Haq (The Absolute Truth) & Al-Hameed (The Praiseworthy);
by the waseelah of Hussain Ash-Shaheed {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Mu’izz (The Honourer and Bestower) & Al-Muzil (The Dishonourer);
by the waseelah of Zain Al Abideen {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Baqee (The Everlasting) & Al-Badee (The Incomparable Originator);
by the waseelah of Baqir Al Uloom {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Jaami (The Gatherer & The Uniter) & Al-Jaleel (The Majestic);
by the waseelah of Jafar Al Sadiq {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Khabeer (The All Aware) & Al-Kabeer (The Most Greatest);
by the waseelah of Musa Al Kazim {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Ar-Ra’oof (The Most Kind) & Ar-Razzaq (The Provider);
by the waseelah of Ali Ibn Musa Al Ridha {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are At-Tawwab (The Ever Pardoning) & Al-Lateef (The Subtle One, The Most Gentle);
by the waseelah of Mohammad Taqi Al Jawad {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Haseeb (The Reckoner) & Al-Hafeedh (The Preserver);
by the waseelah of Ali Naqi Al Hadi {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Al-Ahad (The Unique, The Only One) & Al-Alee (The Most High, The Exalted);
by the waseelah of Hassan Al Askari {a.s}
Ya Allah {SWT} - You are Malik-Ul-Mulk (Master of Kingdom, Owner of Dominion) & Al-Muntaqim (Avenger);
by the waseelah of Mohammad Al Mehdi Al Muntazar {ajf}
Rabbana atina fid dunya hasanatan wa fil Aakhirati hasanatan waqina ‘adhaban-nar – behaqqe Muhamadin wa Alay
Muhammad
"O’ our Lord, grant us good in this world and good in the Hereafter, and save us from the punishment of the
Fire – by the right and status of Muhammad {saws} and the Family of Muhammad {saws}."
